## Residual risks / blocker

The harness failed immediately after its pre-OpenCode-exit UI capture. The exact package requires that captured visible OpenCode text contain `ctrl+d` and an `exit`/`clear/exit` marker. The captured OpenCode UI contained the music row but neither required shortcut string, so `grep -Fq -- 'ctrl+d'` returned nonzero before the normal-exit step. This makes the live certification incomplete; it did not reach final topology cleanup, Apnea-manifest comparison, or Gate C.

Recovery restored media and sent the one allowed `escape` then `ctrl+d` sequence. The OpenCode PID is subsequently absent, but its owned root `/private/var/folders/fh/zx6t2vf55zd3rmf08mrg5jdc0000gn/T/opencode-next-17386.sf5cq0`, runner `/private/var/folders/fh/zx6t2vf55zd3rmf08mrg5jdc0000gn/T/vlc-cert-runner.g3opy7`, and returned tab/panes are deliberately preserved under the package’s failed-certification recovery rule. No further cleanup or retry was performed.
